# The rescue root's packages, beyond mmdebstrap's minbase: read by the image build
# (docs/vip-image.md, "Two roots"), from the pinned snapshot, without recommends. Small and
# rarely changed: it exists to be reachable when the pedal root isn't, and to repair it.

# A different kernel from the pedal's: Ubuntu's plain flavour (rtpi devices/vip/device.env,
# RESCUE_KERNEL), so a problem in one is never in both.
linux-image-7.0.0-1017-raspi
linux-modules-7.0.0-1017-raspi
linux-firmware-raspi
wireless-regdb

# Booting, and changing the boot selection (rtpi's vip-boot).
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
udev
dbus
dracut-core
python3-minimal

# Reaching it: WiFi, a cable, mDNS (resolved), sshd.
openssh-server
sudo
wpasupplicant
iproute2
iputils-ping
ca-certificates

# Repairing the pedal root: check and mount its filesystems, edit, restore its image from
# pedal-data (zstd), and see what's on the card.
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
fdisk
zstd
util-linux
procps
kmod
less
